#: break_taker.lua:13
msgid "Seneca"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:14
msgid "Sometimes even to live is an act of courage."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:16
msgid "Cicero"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:17
msgid ""
"It is not by muscle, speed, or physical dexterity that great things are achieved,\n"
"but by reflection, force of character, and judgment."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:19
msgid "Ovid"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:20
msgid ""
"Dripping water hollows out stone,\n"
"not through force but through persistence."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:22
msgid "Marcus Aurelius"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:23
msgid "Life is a struggle and wandering in a foreign country."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:26
msgid "Hippocrates"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:27
msgid "Let food be thy medicine and medicine be thy food."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:30
msgid "Sun Tzu"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:31
msgid "If quick, I survive. If not quick, I am lost."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:33
msgid "Lao Tzu"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:34
msgid ""
"Fill your bowl to the brim and it will spill.\n"
"Keep sharpening your knife and it will blunt."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:36
msgid "Confucius"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:37
msgid ""
"Learning without thought is labour lost;\n"
"thought without learning is perilous."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:39
msgid "Chongyang"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:40
msgid ""
"Reed-thatched huts and grass-thatched shelters are essential for protecting the body.\n"
"To sleep in the open air or in the open fields offends the sun and moon."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:41
msgid ""
"On the other hand,\n"
"living beneath carved beams and high eaves is also not the action of a superior adept.\n"
"Great palaces and elevated halls,\n"
"— how can these be part of the living plan for followers of the Dao?"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:42
msgid ""
"Medicinal herbs are the flourishing emanations of mountains and waterways,\n"
"the essential florescence of plants and trees."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:43
msgid ""
"Followers of the Dao join together as companions\n"
"because they can assist each other in sickness and disease.\n"
"If you die, I’ll bury you; if I die, you’ll bury me."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:45
msgid "The Dalai Lama"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:46
msgid ""
"If you think you are too small to make a difference,\n"
"try sleeping with a mosquito."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:49
msgid "Masanobu Fukuoka"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:50
msgid ""
"The ultimate goal of farming is not the growing of crops,\n"
"but the cultivation and perfection of human beings."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:52
msgid "Kazuaki Tanahashi"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:53
msgid "Artist's need the world."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:55
msgid "Kobayashi Issa"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:56
msgid ""
"O snail\n"
"Climb Mount Fuji\n"
"But slowly, slowly!"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:59
msgid "Mahatma Gandhi"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:60
msgid ""
"Each night, when I go to sleep, I die.\n"
"And the next morning, when I wake up, I am reborn."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:63
msgid "Saadi"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:64
msgid "Whatever is produced in haste goes hastily to waste."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:67
msgid "Nick Joaquín"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:68
msgid "The point is not how we use a tool, but how it uses us."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:71
msgid "John Plant"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:72
msgid ""
"My approach is to look for what I’m interested in using\n"
"and if it’s there I use it."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:75
msgid "Joss Whedon"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:76
msgid ""
"Humor keeps us alive. Humor and food.\n"
"Don't forget food. You can go a week without laughing."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:78
msgid "Carl Sagan"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:79
msgid ""
"Extinction is the rule.\n"
"Survival is the exception."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:80
msgid "Somewhere, something incredible is waiting to be known."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:81
msgid "If you wish to make an apple pie from scratch, you must first invent the universe."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:83
msgid "Edwin Louis Cole"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:84
msgid ""
"You don't drown by falling in the water;\n"
"you drown by staying there."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:86
msgid "Ernest Hemmingway"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:87
msgid "Never confuse movement with action."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:89
msgid "Kurt Vonnegut"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:90
msgid "A step backward, after making a wrong turn, is a step in the right direction."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:92
msgid "Jane Addams"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:93
msgid ""
"Perhaps nothing is so fraught with significance as the human hand,\n"
"this oldest tool with which man has dug his way from savagery,\n"
"and with which he is constantly groping forward."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:95
msgid "Barry Gehm"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:96
msgid "Any technology distinguishable from magic is insufficiently advanced."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:98
msgid "Bob Ross"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:99
msgid ""
"Lets build a happy little cloud.\n"
"Lets build some happy little trees."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:101
msgid "John Muir"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:102
msgid "The mountains are calling and I must go."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:104
msgid "Ralph Waldo Emerson"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:105
msgid "Adopt the pace of nature: her secret is patience."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:107
msgid "Daniel Boone"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:108
msgid "I've never been lost, but I was mighty turned around for three days once."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:110
msgid "Thomas Edison"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:111
msgid "I have not failed. I've just found 10,000 ways that won't work."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:113
msgid "Woody Allen"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:114
msgid ""
"I'm not afraid of death;\n"
"I just don't want to be there when it happens."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:116
msgid "Bill Watterson"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:117
msgid "Reality continues to ruin my life."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:119
msgid "Oscar Levant"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:120
msgid ""
"There's a fine line between genius and insanity.\n"
"I have erased this line."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:122
msgid "Dr. Seuss"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:123
msgid ""
"They say I'm old-fashioned, and live in the past,\n"
"but sometimes I think progress progresses too fast!"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:126
msgid "Arthur C. Clarke"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:127
msgid "It has yet to be proven that intelligence has any survival value."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:128
msgid ""
"The only way of discovering the limits of the possible\n"
"is to venture a little way past them into the impossible."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:130
msgid "Bear Grylls"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:131
msgid ""
"That fine line between bravery and stupidity is endlessly debated\n"
"– the difference really doesn’t matter."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:133
msgid "Winston Churchill"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:134
msgid "If you're going through hell, keep going"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:136
msgid "George Orwell"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:137
msgid ""
"Progress is not an illusion; it happens,\n"
"but it is slow and invariably disappointing."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:139
msgid "The Black Knight"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:140
msgid "Tis but a scratch!"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:142
msgid "William Shakespeare"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:143
msgid "I like this place and could willingly waste my time in it."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:145
msgid "Isaac Newton"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:146
msgid "Nature is pleased with simplicity. And nature is no dummy."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:148
msgid "Tolkien"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:149
msgid "Not all those who wander are lost."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:151
msgid "Terry Pratchett"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:152
msgid ""
"Give a man a fire and he's warm for a day,\n"
"but set fire to him and he's warm for the rest of his life."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:154
msgid "Douglas Adams"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:155
msgid ""
"Let's think the unthinkable, let's do the undoable.\n"
"Let us prepare to grapple with the ineffable itself, and see if we may not eff it after all."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:157
msgid "Virginia Woolf"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:158
msgid "One cannot think well, love well, sleep well, if one has not dined well."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:160
msgid "Dylan Thomas"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:161
msgid ""
"Do not go gentle into that good night.\n"
"Rage, rage against the dying of the light."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:163
msgid "Robert Swan"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:164
msgid ""
"The greatest threat to our planet\n"
"is the belief that someone else will save it."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:167
msgid "Victor Hugo"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:168
msgid "Emergencies have always been necessary to progress."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:170
msgid "Albert Camus"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:171
msgid "There is scarcely any passion without struggle."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:173
msgid "Marthe Troly-Curtin"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:174
msgid "Time you enjoy wasting is not wasted time."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:177
msgid "Franz Kafka"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:178
msgid "I only fear danger where I want to fear it."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:180
msgid "Friedrich Nietzsche"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:181
msgid "All truly great thoughts are conceived while walking."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:182
msgid "When we are tired, we are attacked by ideas we conquered long ago."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:183
msgid "He who has a strong enough why can bear any how."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:185
msgid "Markus Herz"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:186
msgid ""
"Be careful about reading health books.\n"
"Some fine day you'll die of a misprint."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:189
msgid "Balthasar Gracian"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:190
msgid ""
"There are rules to luck, not everything is chance for the wise;\n"
"luck can be helped by skill."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:193
msgid "Edward de Bono"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:194
msgid ""
"It will be a sinister day when computers start to laugh,\n"
"because that will mean they are capable of a lot of other things as well."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:195
msgid ""
"Po converts what might otherwise be taken as madness\n"
"into a perfectly reasonable illogical procedure."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:198
msgid "Soren Kierkegaard"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:199
msgid "Life can only be understood backwards; but it must be lived forwards."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:226
msgid "BREAK TIME!"
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:228
msgid ""
"You've been here long enough to justify a real break.\n"
"Think of this as a reminder from your better self.\n"
"Go get some rest. Leave Exile behind. You can come back any time."
msgstr ""

#: break_taker.lua:247
msgid "Disable Break-taker popup"
msgstr ""

#: functions.lua:67
msgid "Contains Blanket"
msgstr ""

#: functions.lua:74
msgid "You have no room to hold your blanket, so you drop it."
msgstr ""

#: functions.lua:276
msgid "This bed is already occupied!"
msgstr ""

#: functions.lua:279 functions.lua:290
msgid "Status: Occupied by @1"
msgstr ""

#: functions.lua:376
msgid "Status: Occupied by @1 (old)"
msgstr ""
